  "scope": "The regression executes the checked-out connector/worker shutdown methods and receiver loop, including a real CPU thread and FIFO queue. Device binding, transfer work and the executor boundary are mocked. A test-only abort marker cleans up the original infinite loop after a failing assertion. This proves host thread ownership and shutdown ordering, not device/network shutdown latency. Scope is the modern MooncakeConnector / MooncakePullConnector worker implementation; separate legacy hybrid/layerwise/D2RH implementations are not covered. A transfer stuck inside native I/O can still block drain-and-join; this patch does not add arbitrary I/O cancellation.",
